# Plain punctuation only

When writing copy (README, docs, UI strings, content, comments, etc.), use **plain keyboard punctuation only**.

## Do not use typographic / "smart" punctuation

Avoid:
- Em dash / en dash (Unicode punctuation - avoid U+2014 / U+2013). Use `-` instead.
- Curly quotes / apostrophes (Unicode punctuation - avoid U+201C/U+201D and U+2018/U+2019). Use `"` and `'` instead.
- Ellipsis (Unicode punctuation - avoid U+2026). Use `...` instead.
- Middle dot (Unicode punctuation - avoid U+00B7). Use `.` or `-` instead.
- Any other decorative Unicode punctuation

## Do not use encoded punctuation

Avoid HTML entities for punctuation like:
- `&mdash;`, `&ndash;`, `&hellip;`, `&ldquo;`, `&rdquo;`, `&lsquo;`, `&rsquo;`

## Notes

- Non-English **letters** are fine (e.g. `á`, `ñ`) - this rule is about punctuation, not language.
- If you need a dash, always use the normal hyphen-minus `-`.
